  Stocks This Week- Short Tesla And Buy Apple 
&l;p&g;&l;img class=&q;dam-image shutterstock size-large wp-image-1058307362&q; src=&q;https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/dam/imageserve/1058307362/960×0.jpg?fit=scale&q; data-height=&q;774&q; data-width=&q;960&q;&g; Shutterstock 
Cycles can assist in timing stock purchases. Welcome to the first Stocks This Week column. The underlying cycles concept was explained in a posting on April 6&l;sup&g;th&l;/sup&g;. Software has been directed to plot the most probable course of stock prices over the coming month. The S&a;amp;P 500, the Nasdaq 100 and the Dow Jones Industrials constituents were screened. The results were analyzed to determine the stocks that are most likely to move up or down in the coming week. Here are the results. 
Tesla Motors has generated sixteen trades in the last year. Six of the eight short signals have been profitable. All eight buy signals have been successful. The stock cycle projection points to a decline from April 15&l;sup&g;th&l;/sup&g; through April 24&l;sup&g;th&l;/sup&g;. This provides a shorting opportunity late in the coming week. 
